<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Broad compatibility across modern .NET LTS/STS releases. -->
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>true</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest-recommended</AnalysisLevel>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- ============================ NuGet packaging metadata ============================ -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>PostQuantum.SecureChannel</PackageId>
    <Version>0.3.0-preview.2</Version>
    <FileVersion>0.3.0.2</FileVersion>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.3.0-preview.2: External-review remediation of the protocol glue. Bumps PqProtocol.Version 1 -> 2 (WIRE-FORMAT BREAK; v1 and v2 peers fail cleanly at version negotiation). HKDF info construction is now RFC 5869 / TLS 1.3 HkdfLabel with explicit length framing (Finding 2). Transcript hashing length-prefixes each fragment (Finding 3). Domain-separation labels rebased pqsc/v1 -> pqsc/v2. AntiReplayWindow.Commit enforces the IsAcceptable precondition in code (Finding 1e). Adds five pinned-KAT test files (key schedule, HKDF info bytes, transcript framing, replay-window wrap, record nonce / epoch boundary); 450/450 tests pass on net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0. README gains a prominent preview-and-unaudited status banner; docs/AUDIT-SCOPE.md added. No changes to the X-Wing combiner, ML-DSA-65 signature flow, AES-256-GCM record framing, anti-replay bitmap shape, or the three-message handshake state machine. Adopters running 0.3.0-preview.1 must update both ends to talk again.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Paul Clark</Authors>
    <Company>Paul Clark</Company>
    <Product>PostQuantum.SecureChannel</Product>
    <Description>The high-level post-quantum secure channel library for .NET. Three messages to a live session, mutually authenticated, forward-secret, replay-resistant, transport-agnostic. Built on X-Wing hybrid key agreement (ML-KEM-768 + X25519) and ML-DSA-65 signatures, with AES-256-GCM record encryption. Secure-by-default — algorithms and parameters are fixed; there are no insecure knobs. Includes a Stream adapter, DoS-resistant replay protection, NIST SP 800-38D safety bounds, and built-in observability (EventSource + Meter + ActivitySource). Use this instead of wiring primitives together by hand. Targets net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0.</Description>
    <Summary>High-level post-quantum secure-channel library for .NET. Three-message handshake, mutually authenticated, forward-secret AES-256-GCM sessions over any transport.</Summary>
    <PackageTags>post-quantum;pqc;cryptography;x-wing;xwing;ml-kem;ml-dsa;kyber;dilithium;secure-channel;session;hybrid;kem;encryption;aes-gcm;quantum-safe;mutual-auth;tls-alternative;forward-secrecy;net10</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-securechannel</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-securechannel</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryBranch>main</RepositoryBranch>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Paul Clark</Copyright>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- ============================ Reproducible / source-linked builds ============================ -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Vetted, widely-deployed implementation of ML-KEM, ML-DSA, X25519, and SHA-3/SHAKE.
         X-Wing's combiner is implemented in this library on top of those primitives. -->
    <PackageReference Include="BouncyCastle.Cryptography" Version="2.6.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="PostQuantum.SecureChannel.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
